From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] add riscv64 to the platform tag tables

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted yet: etcd-distro has no riscv64 CI, so a drive-by PR could not be exercised by upstream's own release workflow; needs a maintainer discussion first]

setup.py's platform_ext()/platform_name() map a BUILD_* environment
variable to the etcd release directory name and the PyPI wheel platform
tag. They only know the six platforms upstream's own build-wheels.sh
loop builds for, all backed by prebuilt binaries downloaded from
etcd-io/etcd's own GitHub release (prepare-etcd.sh); etcd-io/etcd
publishes no linux-riscv64 release asset at any version, so this port
cross-compiles etcd/etcdctl/etcdutl from the matching etcd source tag
instead (CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux GOARCH=riscv64 go build, from
./server, ./etcdctl and ./etcdutl) and stages them under the same
etcd/v<version>/etcd-v<version>-linux-riscv64/ layout prepare-etcd.sh
would have produced from a downloaded archive.

Add BUILD_LINUX_RISCV64 -> ("linux-riscv64", "manylinux_2_39_riscv64"),
matching the manylinux_riscv64 image this project's own riscv64 wheel
builds run in (glibc 2.31 is the floor with a riscv64 port; 2.39 is
what the build and test runners carry). Existing platforms resolve
unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 setup.py | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
index 22ca3da..8b79d94 100644
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -25,6 +25,8 @@ def platform_ext():
         return 'linux-ppc64le'
     if os.environ.get('BUILD_LINUX_S390X', None) is not None:
         return 'linux-s390x'
+    if os.environ.get('BUILD_LINUX_RISCV64', None) is not None:
+        return 'linux-riscv64'
     if os.environ.get('BUILD_WIN', None) is not None:
         return 'windows-amd64'
     raise RuntimeError('Set the BUILD_* environment before packaging')
@@ -43,6 +45,8 @@ def platform_name():
         return 'manylinux2014_ppc64le'
     if os.environ.get('BUILD_LINUX_S390X', None) is not None:
         return 'manylinux2014_s390x'
+    if os.environ.get('BUILD_LINUX_RISCV64', None) is not None:
+        return 'manylinux_2_39_riscv64'
     if os.environ.get('BUILD_WIN', None) is not None:
         return 'win_amd64'
     raise RuntimeError('Set the BUILD_* environment before packaging')
--
